This is the 20th or so monk in a long series of monks.  I started them
before my tourist ascension and they died horribly. Then I switched to
a tourist, and ascended. Then went back to monks. These typically died
in the mines, when I would fire sleep at them, a monster would resist,
and I would die next turn.  These problems cleared up when I made a
point of carrying a light source with me in the mines.  Another thing
is I finally gave up trying to work within the monk's skills and just
started carrying a stack of daggers around.  It  also greatly improved
my game.

The second to last one did very well indeed, but died at Master Kaen's
hands because I went to recon that level and didn't realize he'd wake
up the second I set foot on the level. This one was better prepared.

Game-opening break:  Early wand of enlightenment allows me to identify
an early ring of regeneration.  This regen ring kept me alive in many
dangerous situations, including the endgame.

Bonehead move of the game:  Write a scroll of enchant ARMOR instead of
writing a scroll of enchant WEAPON. Read it, and evaporate my +4
fireproof boots of jumping. Very disappointing.

Lesson of the game: You don't need speed boots if you can perform
"haste" at 0% failure.

RNG Generosity:  7 rings of regeneration, 4 magic lamps, each one
yielding a wish.
RNG cheapness:  Not a single scroll of charging or stinking cloud. No
rings of conflict, either.

